# sqlplus (OCI thick) calling a procedure with an OUT parameter against
# Oracle 23ai Free — the 64-bit OCI dialect (the sqlplus bundled in gvenzl/oracle-free:23-slim),
# recorded through dbbat, not through a bare relay: see ociFixtureProvenance.
# One line per server response that opens with the IO vector (TTC message
# 0x0b): the TNS Data payload, two data-flag bytes first, exactly as
# extractTTCPayload receives it.
#
# These carry the same field list the thin recordings do, marshaled in the
# wide/fixed-width OCI encoding — little-endian integers of a per-call-site
# width where a thin client sends compressed ones.
#
# Regenerate with:
#   ORACLE_CAPTURE_OCI_FIXTURES=1 ORACLE_TEST_OCI_CLIENT=container \
#     go test -tags integration -run TestCapture_OCIFixturesThroughDBBat ./internal/proxy/oracle/



